In article <43stgo$62a@news.cic.net>, newsroom <newsroom@cedar.cic.net> writes:
:   Heres a question :   What kind of cartridge tape drive will work
:on a VAX 750?   Having no SCSI controller, it would need to run off
:a UDA50 controller or TU tape controller.    Can a TK50 be used  with
:a 750?

  The VAX-11/750 I/O bus is the UNIBUS and sometimes the Massbus, and
  the internal bus is the CMI.  There is no Digital SCSI controller for
  any of these busses.

  One of the cheapest solutions will involve a new or used VAXstation or
  VAXserver system, DECnet communcations, and (if appropriate) a cluster. 
  One other available alternative is a new or used InfoServer.  (The
  InfoServer is not intended for high-throughput BACKUP operations, but
  the VAX-11/750 likely won't stress it.)  Both of these options assume
  the VAX-11/750 has a DEUNA or (better) DELUA Ethernet controller.

  ------------------------------ Opinionative -------------------------------
