In article <43udl2$a4n@newstand.syr.edu>, kbecker@npac.syr.edu (Kathy Becker) writes:
>
>I have a DECNIS that currently uses a DECstation 5000/120
>as its load host.  It has been suggested that we try the
>Infoserver 150 as a load host since that DECstation has
>started having boot problems of its own.  I've read through
>what little documentation I have, and have not seen any 
>mention of using the Infoserver as a load host.  Does
>anyone know for certain that the Infoserver cannot be used
>as a load host for the DECNIS?
>

	InfoServer can do MOP downline loading by either file name or
ethernet address (aka system id.)  It only does a  simple load of the
image.  The loaded system cannot then request additional information from
the InfoServer.  For example, LPSxx printers go back to the load host for
the date & time.  I don't know what, if anything, a DECNIS requires, so I
can't tell you if it would work for that specific class of devices.

