>I want to (temporarily) use an RZ28 in a storage works cabinet with my
>mac. I have everything cabled OK, but when I try to use the disk the
>mac complains that it's not spun up - obviously I need to tell the RZ28
>to spin up on power on. 

    I found the following information in one of our internal NOTES 
    conferences.  Hope it helps,

    -- Kenny

        There is a set of three jumpers are on the module, near the SCSI
        bus connector.  They control termination and term power.
        To set spinup, look at the other end of the module.
        There are ten jumpers there. the three closest to the corner
        of the module are the ID jumpers.  The seventh from the corner
        is the spin-up jumper.

