In article <DFGt7I.Lnt@didymus.rmi.de> andreas@didymus.rmi.de (Andreas Fassl) wrote:

> The upgrade was done just as the 1.0 -> 1.7 and ended with the message 
> "Please powercycle". So I did. 
> The machine came up with a message ".. 1.9" and after all testing
> and displaying the bios data of the graphics card (ELSA Winner 1000 EISA)
> a blue row appeared on the top of the screen - status: Hang.

OK This is because the ELSA Winner card is not being initialised.
When you switch to the ARC Console the firmware attempts to run the BIOS on
the video card. If the BIOS fails then the system will appear to 'hang'. It 
looks like in your case (and the case of Michael Schwingen - "Alpha PC 150
(Jensen) problems") that the BIOS emulation in V1.9 firmware does not appear
to work with the ELSA Winner card. NOTE: The BIOS emulation is not run by the
SRM Console.


> Now the systems tells me after >>> show config
> DEC 2000 Modell 300 AXP - ROM Version 1.9
> 
> Alpha AXP SRM Firmware Version - 34a
> VMS PAL X5.48/OSF PAL X1.35 - Built on 22-Jun-1995 14:29:30.27
> 
> CPU	OK	EV4	P3.0 6.6ns

You're firmware installation was successful, verified that V1.9 is now installed
in your system. Although the latest release is V1.9, there should be no issues
running current Windows NT versions with Firmware Version V1.7 from the CDROM 
update kit. (V1.5 is the minimum supported revision for Windows NT 3.5 and 3.51).
 

> Another DEC user told me, that the newer firmware versions (>1.7?) are too
> big to fit in the flash ram, so only one console (ARC or SRM) is supported.
> 
> If this is true, how can I use the ECU? It wants to boot in ARC mode, but
> this doesn't work.

This information only applies to the AXP PCI 33 motherboard, which is an Alpha
motherboard for the OEM market. It has 256k of Flash RAM and therefore
contains the Windows NT ARC console, the UNIX SRM Console OR the LINUX
MILO Console at any one time.

This is not the case on the DEC2000 model 300 motherboard. It has a 1Mb FLASH
which holds both ARC Console and SRM Console. Updating the firmware updates both
ARC and SRM. The correct ECU is also required to be run before booting an 
operating system.


In article <44c3ij$14f@nntpd.lkg.dec.com> hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com (Stephen Hoffman) wrote:
>    Neither the ELSA Winner graphics controller nor the SONY CDU-6xx
>    CD-ROM devices are supported by the PALcode.  

Yes, the ELSA Winner card is not supported by Digital. The card will therefore
not have been tested as part of any firmware code verification test.



