sorry to hear it; but that's a sure sign it still isn't set up correctly.


> I concur...  especially when it locks to your account well after you're
> not actually using the compiler, so you have the next programmer waiting
> for a stupid license.  Solution to this stupidity is to kill the license
> manager and restart in some automated fashion, I imagine, but it's really,
