Actually the "socially approved" solution is to set the LINGER value
to something really short (or even zero). The reasons for not doing so
are:

1) If you are doing a series of compilations in a row, nonzero
   linger provides an acceleration for acquisition of tokens.

2) It decreases the load imposed on the network.



