  Nick>   Is it possible to run Unix on these machines? In the recent
  Nick> press release it only mentions Windows NT.

If you do buy an XL in the hope of running Linux/Alpha sometime in the
future, be advised that the Matrox graphics card that comes by default
with this system is not supported by XFree86 (and, according to some
sources, never will be supported because Matrox is following the same
brain-dead path that Diamond used to follow, i.e., they don't disclose
programming info without NDA).  By the same token, I should mention
that Linux/Alpha currently has an X server for S3-based cards only,
but unlike the Matrox case, this should be a temporary restriction
only.

  Nick> The reason I was
  Nick> wondering was because it looks like its based on the AXPpci
  Nick> 233XL motherboard which does support Digital Unix.  (The docs
  Nick> for this were on the German Web site).

As far as I know, the XL is basically a Celebris whose daughterboard
has an Alpha chip (and probably the 2nd-level cache & PCI controller)
instead of an x86.  The daughterboard has a 21064A, and it is
therefore more likely to be similar to the Cabriolet (aka AlphaPC64)
design rather than the AXPpci33.  But I'm guessing here.

	--david



