KDJ11-AB.

Well here you go:

Jumper		Function
_________________________

W1		Set bit 15 of bootstrap start address in power up
		option 3

W2		Set bit 14 of bootstrap address in power up opt 3

W3		Power up option selection bit 0

W4		Set bit 13 of bootstrap address in power op opt 3

W5		Determin repose to halt.  If in then a halt causes
		processor to go to Micro-ODT mode.  If out then trap
		to loc 4 and set bit 7 in cpu error reg

W6		Set bit 12 of bootstrap address in power up opt 3

W7		Power up option selection bit 1

W8		Disable wakeup circuit.  If in the on board wakeup is
		disabled and BDCOK is obtained from an external source.
		If in then the onboard wakeup circuit is used.

W9		BEVENT register enable.  Permits external event interrupt
		request to proc.  If out then BEVENT is recognised and is
		under control of bit 6 of the line time clock reg.  if out
		then BEVENT is disabled and line time clock reg is also
		disabled.

In this W9 is furthest away from the edge connector and W1 is nearest.

The wake up options are:

Option 0	Both W3 and W7 in.  Reads physical memeory locs 24 and 26
		and loads the data into PC and PS.  The processor then
		either services pending interrupts or starts exec where the
		PC points.

option 1	W3 in W7 out.  Unconditionally enters Micro-ODT with PS
		clear.

Option 2	W3 out W7 in.  Bootstrap from PROMs.  KDJ11-AB boot prom
		is not used.  Processor sets PC at 173000 and ps at 340.
		processor then processes pending interrupts or starts
		program exec.

Option 3	W3 out W7 out.  Processor reads the four bits set by W1, W2,
		W4, W6 and loads the result into bits 15 to 12 in PC.
		Bits 11 through 0 of PC are set to 0 and PS is set to 340.
		
