Michael,

The ELSA Winner card is an 'unsupported' card (i.e. unsupported by Digital).
If the card is not initialised by the firmware then the ARC Console cannot be
displayed. It is unlikely that V1.0 firmware can initialise an ELSA winner card
properly. Higher versions of firmware are more likely to be able to initialise it.

On the plus side, the ELSA Winner 1000 is listed on Microsoft's HCL (from Windows
NT 3.5 onwards - Dec '94) for Alpha based systems so it certainly should work if the
firmware can initialise it. I would suspect that we would need V1.5 firmware as a 
minimum for this card to be initiailised correctly. I'll just stress that we
have never tested this card in a DECpc AXP150 system.

Do you have access to a VT Terminal? I'll contact you off-line with detailed
instructions on how to update the firmware.



