I have such a board (bought a complete system): 16 MB  RAM  (you  need  4  PS/2
style SIMMs *with parity*, I am not yet sure if 36 or 40-bit SIMMs are needed).

>- What is the state of Alpha-Linux? Is the kernel-API suficiently
>compatible, so that I can recompile x86-Linux programs?

If the programs are 64-bit-clean, they should compile.

>- What controllers can the Board use to boot? Can it only use the EISA
>Adaptec controller, or can I also use an inexpensive Adaptec ISA
>controller, e.g. an Adaptec 1510? Could I probably use a standard PC
>IDE controller?

AFAIK, the SRM console can not boot from IDE drives - it can't even  boot  from
floppy.

>- Can I use an arbitrary PC graphics card?

I don't think so. The console firmware must support the card (I am just  having
problems after accidentally *down*grading my firmware, so the card  is  no more
recognized).

>- How is Alpha-Linux driver support?

Some work, some don't. Adaptec 1742 is OK, ne2000 seems to work, too. SCSI tape
does not work with 1.3.28.

>- Is it possible to use the board with 64bit memory access (i.e. only
>two PS/2-Simms, instead of four)?

