>   Heres a question :   What kind of cartridge tape drive will work
>on a VAX 750?   Having no SCSI controller, it would need to run off
>a UDA50 controller or TU tape controller.    Can a TK50 be used  with
>a 750?

Yes, you can put a TK50 on a 750; in particular, you'd need the TUK50
Unibus controller for it.  These seem to be pretty rare; I've only
ever seen one in my entire life.

I suppose an even rarer option was the RUX50; the few mentions I've
seen about this unit hint that it drives both RX50 and RX180 floppy
drives.

If the 750 is going to be in operation for much longer into the future,
I'd highly recommend getting some sort of SCSI controller for it.
CMD currently manufactures one, and you may be able to find a Emulex
of Sigma controller from a dealer that handles used equipment.

