We have a DLT-2700 on a 2100 Alpha Server running VMS.  We are quite happy
with it.  I have found that data transfers to it are better than 1.5 MB/sec
in compression mode.  We typically see about 2x to 2.3x compression.

We are considering getting a DLT-6000 (30/60GB) as additional backup device. 
The tape cost is almost a wash though, $35 for CompacTape III versus
$105 for CompacTape IV.  It is just easier to handle one tape versus 2 or
three for a system/cluster backup.  

Since many other companies are selling the DLT, I think it is becoming a
little more accepted.  Also, I heard the a Korean company was licensing with
Quantum as second source.

I am happy with the drive.  For our data system, we are also considering a 
TL820, so we're definately embracing the technology.

