hour).  The "send falure reason" value is 00010000, which according to
the operations guide is a "heartbeat error".

Our DELNI is not hooked to a larger network, it's essentially the hub
of our network.  The switch on the DELNI for "port 9" is set properly.
The system has been working perfectly for about 3 years now.  We have
a MVax 3800, a Vax 4600,a couple of Decserver 200/mc's, and a DEMPR
thinwire repeater feeding our 50+ PC's.  Everything else seems to be
working OK.  I've tried switching the AUI cable and using a different
DELNI port, no change.  Running the Infoserver diagnostics (>>>TEST
50) shows no problem with the Ethernet NI.

If I set the infoserver to use the Thinwire port and attach it to the
DEMPR it seems to work OK, but I'd like to leave it on the DELNI if
possible.  Besides, if the problem is in the infoserver, I'd like to
know so I can try to make arrangements to get it fixed.  (we don' t
have hardware maint on it, so I don't want to send it if there's
nothing wrong).

Any suggestions?

Also, what exactly is the heartbeat for?  I've seen references to it
relating to thickwire & transceivers, but we don't have any thickwire
(except the DELNI) so it's not been anything I've had any experience
with.




