:
:I'm trying to run SLIP into TIA over /dev/tty02 on my VAXstation 3100,
:but the modem keeps over-running the port.  Can someone direct me to a
:pinout of the DECconnect wiring on the back of the 3100?  I hope
:hardware flow control is there somewhere.  The man page for the SS
:device is not very encouraging.

  On the serial port on the VAXstation 3100, there is no hardware flow
  control, and there is no modem control.  (The MicroVAX 3100 differs;
  it does support modem control.)  The silos on most VAX and Alpha
  console ports are not usually very deep; the console ports are not
  designed nor intended for heavy usage.

  The DECconnect MMJ pinout is listed in the OpenVMS FAQ.

