> Related to my earlier question:  I've got a group of DECpcs on Pathworks. 
> I don't know much about 'em, but I'm trying to configure them to run
> winsock.  I've downloaded the 6 files named pw5a_X.exe (where X is 1-6)
> onto the ULTRIX they are networked to, & I plan to x-fer them to the DOS
> partition & run this tomorrow.  These files were at:
> ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/PCI/
>
> If I do this, will my Pathworks be upgraded to run & be Winsock
> compatible?  If not, what else do I need to do to take advantage of
> DOS/Winsoc applications like Netscape
>

I don't think that installing the 5.0a client software will solve your problem,
it is only an update to support a coexistence between the Windows for
Workgroups network and Pathworks. I consider it as more useful to spend the
time installing the 5.1 client which for sure has winsock. If you want to use
Netscape, then you better get pw51_1.exe and pw51_2.exe from the above
mentioned ftp service, it contains ECO3 with modifications to the TCP/IP part
of Pathworks. And you still have to increase the TCPMaxSock entry in pwtcp.ini
because the sockets are closed with a too high delay and otherwise Netscape
'hangs' after some time. The latter hints are not my own experiences but
results from monitoring the newsgroup vmsnet.networks.desktop.pathworks.

