sounds like you would need at least a small jukebox because a single platter
will not backup your 5 gig.  Writing to MO is dog slow.  With DLT2000 tape
drives coming in at about $3k I think that is your best bet.  DLTs are fast
and reliable.
 
3rd party in the MO world can be a disaster.  DEC software is well worth the
money.  3rd party software (especially from an un-named East Coast outfit) can
make you wish you never heard of MO.
 
The previous kluge that I worked with resulted in data corruption and a vendor
that refused to take any responsibility.  That MO jukebox was later sold on the
used market and replace with a unit from DEC.
 
Seriously looked at DLT before you buy into MO.  If you do buy an MO system
I suggest you get a 30-day money back option on the purchase contract.  Then
test it, benchmark it, and then decide if you really want to do MO backups.
 
Good luck, Doug



