Hi;

  I have several HP JetDirect cards in LJ4's and LJ4+'s and have no
problems with any of them except in one case.  All of the cards have
firmware revision A.02.01 except for a newer one which has revision
A.03.06.  We are a mostly UNIX TCP/IP network but we have two legacy
VAXes at VMS 5.5.

  The problem only occurs when the VAXes print to the newer JD card.
The VAXes are using the "steam protocol" to connect to the cards'
port 9100.  These jobs often get "lost" in route from the VAXes to 
the card, that is, the administrator of the VAXes says that the jobs
have definitly left her spoolers but nothing comes out of the printer.
On one occaision just after a job was "lost", we observed the Laser 
Jet to display error code 40, implying that a job was cut off in the
middle.

  Unfortunently, I am not up on VAXes and the administrator of the
VAXes cannot tell me much about the stream protocol.  Can anyone
give me a hint about what might be wrong in the configuration of
either the VAXes or the JetDirect cards?

  My first workaround for the problem was to use the newer card's
LPD server abilities but this idea is bad for us since we _must_
have a detailed burst page printed with each job.
 
