That rumor that you've heard is not true.  Since DEC is (well, was) in the
business of selling drives to the OEM market, that is just a silly idea.

Anyway, here's the jumper layout of the RZ25:

    *-----------------------*	      	J5	
    |                 54321 |	SCSI ID	P1 P2 P3
    |1 J6               J7  |      0	 -  -  -   - OUT
    |2                      |	   1	 -  -  X   X IN
    |3                      |	   2	 -  X  -
    |4                      |	   3	 -  X  X
    |5                      |	   4	 X  -  -
    |6                      |	   5	 X  -  X
    |7                      |	   6	 X  X  -
    |8                      |	   7	 X  X  X
    |                      3|
    |                   J5 2|	J6 P1	Self Test (Default OUT)
    |                      1|	   P2	Spin Up Immediately (OUT)
    |                       |		Wait for command (IN)
    | SCSI connector  Power |	   P4	Write Protect (OUT)
    *-----------------------*	   P5	parity Check Enable (IN)
    				   P6	Drive Powers SCSI TERMPWR (IN)		
    				   P7	Drive Powers Internal Terminator (IN)
    				J7 P4	Spindle Lock (IN)
    				   P5	Remote LED (OUT)

