Drives that DEC sells, such as RZ28, may be manufactured by Seagate
but they have been certified by DEC and may possibly have had the
firmware changed before DEC resells them.  According to the person at
DEC I talked to, most drives that properly support the SCSI-2 spec
will work OK, but just because a RZ28 says "Seagate" on the drive does
not mean it's the same as an off-the-shelf Seagate drive.





