In article <4325fs$auu@terby.do.open.de>, andreas@terby.do.open.de (Andreas Terbrack) writes:

:I've been offered a TK50Z-F3 for cheap and would like to connect it
:two a MicroVAX 3100/10. I know that the matching Drive for a 3100
:is the TK50Z-G3, and that the F3 normaly belongs to a MicroVAX/
:VAXStation 2000.
:
:Can anybody tell me:
:- what the differences between F3/G3 are ?
:
:- if it is possible to connect this drive to 
:  a '3100 (perhaps with some mods to cables/connectors or
:  replacing the Firmware with one from a G3) ?

  The VAXstation 2000 series didn't have/use a SCSI bus, and different
  ROMS are needed to correctly operate the TK50Z on the VAXstation 3100
  series SCSI bus.

  I believe the replacement ROM part number is/was 23-453E6-00.  You may
  (will) need to remove the termination pack from the F3 drive etch, you
  will need SCSI cables (duh! :-), and you will need to reset the drive
  addressing from unit 1 (typical of the 2000) to 5 (typical of the 3100).

  I would not try any of this if I weren't prepared to `trash' the drive
  should the drive get permanently messed up, and if I weren't equipped
  and trained to work with etch and with static-sensitive components.
  Given a choice, I'd get a TK30 or (better) a TLZ0% DDS (4mm) drive.

  ------------------------------ Opinionative -------------------------------
   Stephen Hoffman      OpenVMS Engineering      hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com
