Beth Paxton <bpaxton@dvorak.amd.com> wrote:
>
>We have been loaned an alpha 250.  It looks like the ethernet
>interface is 'tu0', however we are unable to get this system to
>talk on the net -- no packets in or out.  We can 'ping' the system

You may need to tell the tu0 interface what kind of physical network
you're on.  From the srm console prompt (the >>> prompt that you get
when the machine is powered on in unix/vms mode) type 'set ewa0_mode
BLAH' where BLAH is AUI, Twisted-Pair or BNC.   Actually, really
typing BLAH should get you a list of valid options.

