We use CD-R for archiving and database distribution. We have not had any
problems with RRD42 or RRD43 as used on Ultrix and OSF/1.

From our experience it does appear that there is something "inferior"
with CD-R disks in that occasionally we find a drive that either
refuses to read the disk or gives read-errors. I seems that if
something in the drive is starting to fail or is slightly out of spec
it will read normal CD's OK but have problems with CD-R.

There is a fundamental problem in putting PC style CD-Drives on Ultrix
and OSF/1 and I believe VMS (but might be wrong) in that PC's use a
block size of 2048 bytes but Unix/VMS use 512. I have managed to get
the Unix drivers to issue a set block size command when the disk is
mounted and have a toshiba drive working on OSF/1 but would have no
idea on VMS.

