organization: Digital Equipment Corp
reply-to: hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com (Stephen Hoffman)
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


In article <DEo70p.69L@freenet.carleton.ca>, ax436@FreeNet.Carleton.CA
(Tareef Attar) writes:

:Anyone out there has a good book on VAX MACRO-11 programming like the one
:by Sara Baase. If have one for sale or if you know were I can find it, please
:let me know. 

  I assume you mean VAX Macro (Macro-32), not the PDP-11 macro assembler.

  There are two Digital Press books out on the topic of `low-level' VAX
  architecture and programming, one is the _Computer Programming and
  Architecture_ textbook, second edition, Levy & Eckhouse, (EY-6740E-DP),
  and the other is the _VAX Architecture Reference Manual_, also second
  edition, Brunner, (EY-F576E-DP).  Both are available from Digital Press.

  Also possibly of some interest will be the OpenVMS Programming Guide
  (part of the OpenVMS documentation set) and the VAX Macro manual (part
  of the OpenVMS VAX documentation).

  I would generally avoid programming in Macro in favor of C or similar
  language, save for in those (very) few specific areas where Macro is
  particularly suited.  And one can perform mixed-language programming
  quite easily under OpenVMS.
  
  ------------------------------ Opinionative -------------------------------
   Stephen Hoffman      OpenVMS Engineering      hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com
