> :Would someone please tell me the specs for the keyboard jack on the back of a 
> :VT220 terminal?  It takes a telephone type of connector, and I just wonder
> :what the different wires do.
> 
>   You'll need access to the keyboard hardware specifications.  (The brains
>   of the VT220 are not in the keyboard -- the VT220 keyboard controller and
>   the LK201 keyboard use a low-level serial protocol to communicate.) 

The keyboard interface is described in chapter 6 of the Pro350 technical
manual. The four pins are +12, ground, serial out, and serial in. The manual
doesn't say what's on which pin, but a few minutes of poking around with
a voltmeter should uncover that. The serial data is RS-232; I left the book
in the other room and promptly forgot the baud rate...
