richardp@iinet.com.au (Richard Paton) writes:

>It's a AXP VME64.  Noone at DEC seems to think that shared memory is 
>available (other than through I/O)

>>>I'm new to VME stuff, but need to write a device driver that accesses 
>>>shared memory on the VME bus (we've got a comms card that can share its 
>>>memory on the bus).  I've been told that the only way that the Alpha 
>>>processor can access this memory-on-the-bus is by DMA.  Is this true? or 
>>>can the alpha access this shared memory as if it were local.

>>>If DMA is the only method, what other methods are available to 
>>>communicate with devices on the VME bus?

   You can communicate with VME devices using three different methods:

      -- PIO:  Use vba_map_csr() to map the VME region and then use
	       write_io_port() and read_io_port().

      -- DMA:  Use vba_set_dma_addr(), dma_map_alloc(), dma_map_load()
	       to set up.  Use vba_dma() for the transfers.

      -- Memory Mapped:  Map the region using vba_map_csr() and then
	       use iohandle_to_phys() and PHYS_TO_KSEG() to get the
	       page frame number.

