Thanks,  I have already found the solution to get *BOTH* boards working. 
 The isacfg program actually needs more than just the irq.  It also needs 
the iobase address used by the first dip switch.  Also, the 
isa_config.dat file in VMS can only refer to slots 1 thriugh 4 on the isa 
bus.  Even though you can configure isacfg for any slot (6,10 whatever), 
you must use 1,2,3 or 4!

Also, in order to get the second board to work, I had to disable the 
onboard COM2, and steal it's interrupt.

Just a note: The isacfg documentation should also include a sample to 
configure the Digiboard.

Thanks again,

Rob Grimm




