I'm having a problem with using SCSI disks from an Ultrix
DECstation on a Macintosh.  In particular, the disks are 
rz25, rz56, and rz57.  The problem is that on a DECstation, 
unlike most other systems, the disks do not automatically 
spin up on power up.  When the boot command is issued, the 
DECstation sends a signal to spin up the disk.  However, on 
a Mac, no such signal is sent out because Mac disks are already
spinning at bootup.  Because of this problem, the Mac Os
doesn't recognize the SCSI disk.

I've been told that there is a disk utility for Ultrix
called 'scu'.  I looked at it but couldn't find anything
useful for what I'm trying to accomplish.

If you know any helpful info, please email me.  Thanks.

