tapes from other 8mm drives.  I have on occasion had to try an 8mm tape
received from elsewhere on as many as 4 drives before I found one that
could read it.

All that said, if you only need the 8mm for occasional data transfer, then
it will probably work, at least for an 8200.  There are apparently
differences in how one sets compression on the other model drives - not
sure since we don't have those. 

However, if you really have any choice in the matter, go with DLT.  
Everybody I've had mail from who's compared the two has found DLT vastly
superior to 8mm.

Regards,

David Mathog
