johnson@atc.ameritel.net wrote:
>Hello,
>
>I have some hex patterns which represent 64-bit floating point values on a VAX. What I need is to convert them 
>to 64-bit floats on a Motorola processor (IEEE standard float, 11-bit mantissa). 

There are several factors to look for. First, the VAX formats are laid 
out for 16-bit contiguity. So, you have to swap the 16-bits words around. 
Secondly, VAX G uses an exponent bias of 1024, while IEEE uses 1023. 
Furthermore, VAX fraction is .1fff..., IEEE is 1.ffff...

Might help if you looked at a VAX Architecture Handbook.




