In article <42g1hm$c4k_001@news.fast.net>, kshuff@fast.net (kshuff) writes:
:This is another plea for help with a VAX 11/750. The problem is with the 
:console terminal, it will receive data but it will not transmit. Is this a 
:hardware problem or is it in the code itself. All the remote terminals work 
:fine. What physically drives the console, I was told it was the TU58 board but 
:I cannot find any serial devices that drive the console. Any and all help 
:would greatly be appreciated. Thanks

  This sounds like a bad connection on the serial cable, but could also
  indicate a problem on the terminal speed, on the terminal's serial line
  transmitter, on the console's serial line receivers, a broken wire in
  the cable, or an incorrectly wired cable. 

  Check the terminal and host serial line speeds and the stop bit, character
  bit size and related terminal settings.  Try another (known-good) terminal.
  If that doesn't work, try a different cable.  If that doesn't work, try the
  terminal and the cable on another system.  If that _does_ work and
  everything else does _not_ work, you'll need to get somebody to take a
  look at the console serial line interface on the VAX-11/750.

