   Hi.
 Putting xhost + is really quite dangerous...
 However, you can put a more secure statement in your .X11Startup (it is 
allways run when the users X section is started). For example, in my 
case:

# Sample /usr/users/npll/.X11Startup file
# I take no responsability on this...!
(/usr/bin/X11/xhost +another_machine)
(/usr/bin/X11/xhost +yet_another_machine)

 This is safer than just oppening your display to the world...
 And remember, if someone screws up your display, you can allways make:

 /usr/bin/X11/xhost -

     Good luck...!

