if the tar has been written on the same machine (but running OSF/1 - I
do have a dual boot machine). Current knowledge is that the NT tape
driver is very primitive. As I understand the block-size needs to be a
power of 2. So writting the tar-tape on the SGI with a block-size of
something like 16*512 (tar -cb 16 ...) should eventually help. Please
note that You have to indicate this blocksize while reading the tape.
