>Thank's in advance
>

The critical command is SET MAGTAPE/SKIP, consult the VMS HELP.

On one occasion I had a Tape-Stretcher-11 (TS-11, 45 ips 1600 bpi)
9-track that was "polishing the heads" while re-trying the failing
read operation.  I ended up using CTRL-Y, then SPAWN, then skipping
bad blocks, then logout of the SPAWN, then CONTINUE.  BACKUP tried 
very hard to read the correct block, so that I sometimes had to 
skip several to persuade it not to rewind the tape a ways, thereby
getting stuck on the same old bad section. 

If you do this, it is wisest to do it on a hardcopy console or from
a SET HOST/LOG session, and use the restoration command BACKUP/LOG,
because the last file before the bad spot and the first file after
the bad spot may be corrupted - often being the correct size but
with missing blocks filled with zeros.

