Subject: xc/programs/Xserver/hw/dec : R6 Pmax-MFB code broken.
Date: Thu, 02 Jun 1994 16:27:28 -0400
Message-ID: <14353.770588848@MOORE.FAC.CS.CMU.EDU>
From: Dale Moore <Dale_Moore@MOORE.FAC.CS.CMU.EDU>


     VERSION:

R6, public-patch-1

     CLIENT MACHINE and OPERATING SYSTEM:

	DECstation 3100 Ultrix 4.3a

     DISPLAY TYPE:

	PMAX-MFB

     WINDOW MANAGER:

	uwm or Not Applicable

     COMPILER:

native cc

     AREA:

xc/programs/Xserver  Xdec

     SYNOPSIS:

The R6 Xdec server does not work with Monochrome frame buffers.

     DESCRIPTION:

The R6 Xdec X server assumes that the default colormap is writeable.
In routine fbInitProc it attempts to AllocColor even when we have
a Static color map.  Since it can't allocate a color out of the
static colormap, it assumes that it can't initialize the frame buffer
and fails.

If you'll compare the R5 and R6 dec/ws/cfbinit.c you should see in R5
where we either call mfbCreateDefColormap or we do something very similar to
cfbCreateDefColormap .  But in R6 we always do the thing that it similar to
the cfbCreateDefColormap, which does not work on machines with Static
Colormaps.

     REPEAT BY:

Run R6 on a DEC pmax-mfb.  I suspect that you will get the
error 
	Could not AddScreen, ID = PMAX-MFB

	Fatal server error:
	no screens found


     SAMPLE FIX:

*** /afs/cs/local/X11/src/xc/programs/Xserver/hw/dec/ws/cfbinit.c	Sun Apr 17 20:29:54 1994
--- cfbinit.c	Thu Jun  2 15:55:56 1994
***************
*** 1,3 ****
--- 1,9 ----
+ /*
+  * HISTORY
+  * Dale Moore  02-Jun-1994  Carnegie Mellon University
+  *   Changed to work on mfb.  Don't AllocColor if mfb.
+  * $Log$
+  */
  /* $XConsortium: cfbinit.c,v 1.7 94/04/17 20:29:53 dpw Exp $ */
  /***********************************************************
  
***************
*** 405,410 ****
--- 411,423 ----
      {
  	return FALSE;
      }
+ 
+     if (dd->depth == 1)
+     {
+         mfbCreateDefColormap(pScreen);
+     }
+     else
+     {
          /* copy of cfbCreateDefColormap, except variable colors */
          for (pVisual = pScreen->visuals;
  	     pVisual->vid != pScreen->rootVisual;
***************
*** 424,429 ****
--- 437,443 ----
  	    return FALSE;
          }
          (*pScreen->InstallColormap)(pCmap);
+     }
  
      planemask_addr = dd->plane_mask;
      



