It depends on exactly what "error" you got (and I don't have the manual to hand) 
but the classic mistake is to forget to put grant cards in the right places
on the backplane (i.e. leave no empty slots between the KDA50 and the CPU).

There are also one or two "jumpers" that may need to be cut or not cut depending
on the backplane ... for Q/Q slots (which is what you will be using on BA23
and BA123 boxes) I think W22 & W23 (or whatever they are) should be installed.

They can't all be broken can they :-)

Send mail if the above is not enough to pin it down and I'll dig out the manual.
Be sure to describe the error fully ... there are some LEDs on the front (I
think) and the manual calls out the specific errors in some detail.

