In article <42g1hm$c4k_001@news.fast.net>, kshuff <kshuff@fast.net> wrote:
>This is another plea for help with a VAX 11/750. The problem is with the 
>console terminal, it will receive data but it will not transmit. Is this a 
>hardware problem or is it in the code itself. All the remote terminals work 
>fine. What physically drives the console, I was told it was the TU58 board but 
>I cannot find any serial devices that drive the console. Any and all help 
>would greatly be appreciated. Thanks
>
>-Keith S. Huff
>
> kshuff@fast.net

Before diving in to replace the EIA RS-232 line drivers, I'd check some things:

1.  Is the front panel key-switch set to "local" or "remote"?  You have
to use the corresponding console jack - if you've got the wrong one,
then you may see exactly what you are seeing.

2.  If "remote", you might want to try feeding modem control signals
into the console jack.  This position was designed for use with a
modem, after all.

3.  Which operating system are you running?  Under VMS, you ought
to be able to log in to the console terminal after booting.  I don't
know about other operating systems.

Tim. (shoppa@altair.krl.caltech.edu)



