In article <42f657$oef@charm.magnus.acs.ohio-state.edu>, JONESD@kcgl1.eng.ohio-state.edu (David Jones) writes:
|> In message <4289kh$hv6@bcarh8ab.bnr.ca>, smiller@bnr.ca (Scott Miller) writes:
|> >I wrote a simple program that spawns off a thread to act as an RPC server.
|> >It core dumps...
|> 
|> Most likely the RPC server function overflows the stack in your created
|> thread.

Yep, that was it.  I was so busy worrying about the libraries that I forgot
about the (default) 21K stack.  It made sense too, because the output of 
tstack in dbx was truncated for one of the threads, which should have
clued me in to a stack problem.  (Or maybe that had nothing to do with it)

Anyway, thanks for the help.  It was appreciated.
